{"id":"1419b236-9963-4432-a83e-82266b811345","object":"chat.completion","created":1784885401,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    lines = case.get('lines', [])\\n    trajectory = []\\n    for line in lines:\\n        if ':' in line:\\n            parts = line.split(':', 1)\\n            typ = parts[0].strip()\\n            content = parts[1].strip()\\n        else:\\n            typ = line.strip()\\n            content = ''\\n        trajectory.append({'type': typ, 'content': content})\\n    valid = True\\n    error_line = None\\n    if not trajectory:\\n        valid = False\\n        error_line = 0\\n    else:\\n        allowed_next = {\\n            'Thought': {'Action', 'Final'},\\n            'Action': {'Observation'},\\n            'Observation': {'Thought'},\\n            'Final': set()\\n        }\\n        if trajectory[0]['type'] != 'Thought':\\n            valid = False\\n            error_line = 0\\n        else:\\n            for i in range(len(trajectory) - 1):\\n                cur = trajectory[i]['type']\\n                nxt = trajectory[i+1]['type']\\n                if nxt not in allowed_next.get(cur, set()):\\n                    valid = False\\n                    error_line = i+1\\n                    break\\n        if valid and trajectory[-1]['type'] != 'Final':\\n            valid = False\\n            error_line = len(trajectory)-1\\n    return {\\n        'valid': valid,\\n        'error_line': error_line,\\n        'trajectory': trajectory\\n    }\\n\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) for task AGENT-RA-01. The case payload has a \"lines\" list of strings. We need to parse these lines as a trajectory of steps. The task appears to be about agent reasoning with steps: Thought, Action, Observation, Final? The output schema expects \"valid\" (boolean), \"error_line\" (null or integer), and \"trajectory\" (list of objects with \"content\" and \"type\").\n\nWe need to infer the logic. Looking at the fixtures:\n\nCase b-000: lines = [\"Thought: inspect\",\"Action: lookup\",\"Observation: found\",\"Thought: answer\",\"Final: done\"]\nCase b-001: lines = [\"Thought: inspect\",\"Action: lookup\",\"Thought: invalid order\",\"Thought: answer\",\"Final: done\"]\nCase b-002: same as b-001.\n\nInterpretation: The agent should follow a pattern: Thought, Action, Observation, Final? But in b-001, after Action we have another Thought (invalid order). That might be an error. Possibly the allowed sequence is: Thought, Action, Observation, Thought, Final? Actually typical ReAct pattern: Thought -> Action -> Observation -> ... -> Final. But the \"Final\" step likely ends the trajectory. In b-000, it's Thought, Action, Observation, Thought, Final. That's fine. In b-001, after Action we have another Thought instead of Observation. That might be invalid. So we need to validate the sequence.\n\nThe output schema: \"valid\" boolean, \"error_line\" integer (line index where error occurs) or null if valid, and \"trajectory\" array of steps.\n\nWe need to parse each line. The line format seems to be \"Type: content\". For example \"Thought: inspect\" -> type=\"Thought\", content=\"inspect\". But note: \"Final: done\" -> type=\"Final\", content=\"done\". Also \"Observation: found\" -> type=\"Observation\", content=\"found\". So we split on first colon? But careful: content might contain colons? Probably not. We'll split on ': ' (colon space) or just first colon. Safer: split once on ': '.\n\nWe need to validate the sequence. Possibly the rules: The sequence must start with \"Thought\". Then alternate: after Thought, can be Action or Observation? Actually typical ReAct: Thought -> Action -> Observation -> Thought -> ... -> Final. But Final is a special end. Also \"Action\" must be followed by \"Observation\"? In b-001, after \"Action: lookup\" we have \"Thought: invalid order\" - that's invalid because Action must be followed by Observation. So error_line would be the index of the offending line? Or the line after? We need to decide.\n\nLook at b-001: lines[0]=\"Thought: inspect\", lines[1]=\"Action: lookup\", lines[2]=\"Thought: invalid order\". If rule: Action must be followed by Observation, then error at line 2 (index 2). So error_line=2. For b-000, no error, error_line=null.\n\nBut also consider \"Final\" - it should be the last step and only appear once. And it should be preceded by something (Thought?). In b-000, Final is preceded by Thought. That seems fine.\n\nWe need to implement logic that checks the sequence. Also the trajectory should include all lines, even those that are invalid? The output trajectory must include all steps? The schema says items have content and type. So we should parse each line into a step object, regardless of validity. Then the validation checks the sequence and if invalid, set valid=false and error_line to the index of the invalid step (the first violation). If valid, error_line=null.\n\nDefine allowed transitions? Probably: Step types are: Thought, Action, Observation, Final. Possibly also other? In fixtures only these. The pattern: Start with Thought. Then allowed next: after Thought -> Action or Observation? Actually typical ReAct: Thought then Action (to act) then Observation, then Thought again, etc. But sometimes thought can be followed by thought? Not typical. In b-001, after Action, we have Thought, which is invalid. So rule: After Action, must be Observation. After Observation, must be Thought (or Final? Possibly if final observation leads to Final? But in b-000, after Observation we have Thought, then Final. So after Observation, next can be Thought. After Thought, next can be Action. Also after Thought, could it be Final? Yes, in some cases, but in b-000 Final is after Thought, but the Thought before Final is \"Thought: answer\", so that is allowed. So we need to define a state machine.\n\nLet's define possible sequence: \n- First step must be \"Thought\".\n- Then alternating: Thought -> Action -> Observation -> Thought -> ... until Final.\n- Final can only appear after a Thought (or after Observation? Possibly but not in fixtures). In b-000, Final after Thought. In b-001, Final after Thought (at line 4). So rule: Final must be preceded by Thought. Also Final must be the last step, no steps after.\n- Also, no step type can appear out of order.\n\nDefine allowed next types:\n- After Thought: Action or Final (maybe also Observation? Thought->Observation would skip action, maybe not allowed). In typical ReAct, Thought leads to Action (decision), not directly Observation. So we'll assume Thought -> Action or Thought -> Final (if final answer).\n- After Action: Observation (must).\n- After Observation: Thought (or possibly Final? If observation is final answer? Usually not, but could be. We'll allow Thought only, as fixtures show Thought after Observation).\n- After Final: end, no more steps.\n\nAlso, check that Final appears exactly once and at end.\n\nAdditionally, the type string should match exactly: \"Thought\", \"Action\", \"Observation\", \"Final\". If a line doesn't start with one of these, it's invalid, but fixtures seem consistent.\n\nNow implement solve(case):\n- Get lines from case['lines']\n- Initialize trajectory list.\n- For each line, split on first ': ' (or on ':' and strip). But careful: content might contain extra spaces. Use line.split(':', 1) and then strip both parts. But the format seems \"Type: content\". So we'll get type = part0.strip(), content = part1.strip().\n- Append {\"type\": type, \"content\": content} to trajectory.\n- Then validate sequence:\n   - Set valid = True, error_line = None\n   - Define allowed_next map: {\n        \"Thought\": {\"Action\", \"Final\"},\n        \"Action\": {\"Observation\"},\n        \"Observation\": {\"Thought\"},\n        \"Final\": set()  # no next\n     }\n   - Check first step type \"Thought\". If not, error on line 0.\n   - For i from 0 to len(trajectory)-2:\n        current_type = trajectory[i]['type']\n        next_type = trajectory[i+1]['type']\n        if next_type not in allowed_next.get(current_type, set()):\n            valid = False\n            error_line = i+1  # the index of the offending next step? Usually the error is on the step that violates the sequence, i.e., the second step in the pair. So error_line = i+1.\n            break\n   - Also check that Final appears exactly once and is the last step. If Final appears in middle, that's also an error. For example, if Final then something else, error on that something else. Our loop will catch that because after Final, allowed_next is empty, so any next step is invalid.\n   - If no error, valid=True.\n- Return {\"valid\": valid, \"error_line\": error_line, \"trajectory\": trajectory}\n\nNote: The trajectory includes all lines even if invalid. The spec says \"trajectory\" items have content and type. That's fine.\n\nEdge cases: What if there are no lines? Then trajectory empty, first step missing, so error on line 0? But fixtures have lines. We'll handle: if empty trajectory, valid=False, error_line=0? Or maybe null? Better to follow pattern: if no lines, first step not Thought, error_line=0.\n\nNow implement in Python.\n\nAlso need to handle that case payload only has \"lines\" and \"_case_nonce\". We don't need nonce.\n\nWrite solve function:\n\ndef solve(case):\n    lines = case.get('lines', [])\n    trajectory = []\n    for line in lines:\n        # Split on first colon\n        if ':' in line:\n            parts = line.split(':', 1)\n            typ = parts[0].strip()\n            content = parts[1].strip()\n        else:\n            # If no colon, treat whole line as type? Not expected.\n            typ = line.strip()\n            content = ''\n        trajectory.append({\"type\": typ, \"content\": content})\n    # Validate\n    valid = True\n    error_line = None\n    if not trajectory:\n        valid = False\n        error_line = 0\n    else:\n        allowed_next = {\n            \"Thought\": {\"Action\", \"Final\"},\n            \"Action\": {\"Observation\"},\n            \"Observation\": {\"Thought\"},\n            \"Final\": set()\n        }\n        # Check first\n        if trajectory[0]['type'] != \"Thought\":\n            valid = False\n            error_line = 0\n        else:\n            for i in range(len(trajectory) - 1):\n                cur = trajectory[i]['type']\n                nxt = trajectory[i+1]['type']\n                if nxt not in allowed_next.get(cur, set()):\n                    valid = False\n                    error_line = i+1\n                    break\n        # Additional: if no error, verify that Final is last and only once. Ideally it's covered by loop: after Final, any next is invalid. But also ensure there is exactly one Final and it is last. If there is no Final, is that valid? In the pattern, the trajectory should end with Final. But fixtures end with Final. Possibly the task expects that trajectory must end with Final. Check fixtures: b-000 ends with Final, b-001 ends with Final. So likely required. We'll add check: last step must be Final. If not, error on last step or after? We'll set error_line to len(trajectory)-1 if last step not Final.\n        if valid and trajectory[-1]['type'] != \"Final\":\n            valid = False\n            error_line = len(trajectory)-1\n        # Also check that Final appears only once? Already handled because after Final cannot have another, so if second Final appears, error on that step.\n    return {\n        \"valid\": valid,\n        \"error_line\": error_line,\n        \"trajectory\": trajectory\n    }\n\nThat should produce correct results for fixtures:\n- b-000: valid=True, error_line=None, trajectory with 5 steps.\n- b-001: at i=1 (Action) -> next (i=2) is Thought, not Observation => error_line=2, valid=False.\n- b-002: same.\n\nNow output as JSON string with key \"implementation\". Must escape properly.\n\nWrite the Python source as a string. Use triple quotes? But need to escape newlines. Use json.dumps to escape.\n\nThe response must be exactly one JSON object: {\"implementation\": \"<escaped source>\"}. No trailing text.\n\nI'll produce that."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":917,"completion_tokens":2770,"total_tokens":3687,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":896},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":2414},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":896,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":21},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}